## Summary
Adds `UNCHANGED` status to the diff procedure to include nodes that exist in both versions with identical content.

## Problem
When diffing C structs (e.g., Windows PDB types), only changed fields were returned. This made it impossible to reconstruct the complete struct for display in editors.

## Solution
Added a 4th case to handle nodes with matching hashes:
- `NEW`: Node only in diffee
- `MOD`: Node in both, different hashes
- `DEL`: Node only in base
- `UNCHANGED`: **NEW** - Node in both, identical hashes

## Changes

### 1. DiffStatus Enum
Added `UNCHANGED` value and updated error message.

### 2. Opt-in Behavior
```java
private boolean shouldIncludeStatus(DiffStatus status, Set<DiffStatus> statusFilter) {
    if (status == DiffStatus.UNCHANGED) {
        // UNCHANGED requires explicit opt-in (not included in empty filter)
        return statusFilter.contains(status);
    }
    return statusFilter.isEmpty() || statusFilter.contains(status);
}
```

### 3. Handle Identical Hashes
```java
} else if (baseInfo != null && diffeeInfo != null && baseInfo.hash.equals(diffeeInfo.hash)) {
    // UNCHANGED case - node exists in both with identical hash
    if (shouldIncludeStatus(DiffStatus.UNCHANGED, statusFilter)) {
        results.add(new DiffResult("UNCHANGED", baseInfo.label, currentPath,
                baseInfo.properties, diffeeInfo.properties));
    }
    // No recursion needed - children are guaranteed identical by hash
}
```

## Backward Compatibility
✅ Empty `statusFilter` returns only NEW, MOD, DEL (current behavior)  
✅ UNCHANGED requires explicit opt-in via `statusFilter: ["UNCHANGED"]`  
✅ No breaking changes

